Rem ==================================================================
Rem random.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: random numbers
Rem
Rem Built directly on the Rnd builtin (uniform, [0,1), impure — effects
Rem live at the edge, same as Print). Seedless by construction: Rnd
Rem draws from the engine's own auto-seeded generator, so there is no
Rem seed to create, store, or thread through your program — the cost
Rem of that convenience is the one property this whole language is
Rem built to guarantee everywhere else. Random() is NOT a pure
Rem function: calling it twice with identical arguments can (and
Rem should) give two different answers. A fully pure alternative is
Rem possible (an explicitly-seeded generator that threads its state
Rem through every call, the way Isam threads its handle) but that's
Rem the opposite of seedless, so it isn't what's below.
Rem ==================================================================

Rem ---- the builtin this machine is built on --------------------------
Rem
Rem NOT a Def. The engine dispatches it, and a Def whose name is a
Rem builtin is refused; it is written here because random.shoddy is
Rem where a reader goes looking for it. The flat reference is section 10
Rem of docs/spec.html, and the stack effect below is the one the
Rem compiler's own Effects.cs table declares.

Rem Rnd() As Number                                   ( -- x )
Rem     A uniform random number in [0, 1) — zero possible, one never.
Rem     IMPURE, in the same way Print is: calling it twice gives two
Rem     different answers, and it is the single reason nothing in this
Rem     machine is a pure function. It draws from the engine's own
Rem     auto-seeded generator, which is what "seedless by construction"
Rem     above means: there is no generator state for a program to hold.

Rem SEED IS NOT HERE, and its absence is the point of the header above.
Rem Seed(n) reseeds this same generator, so it does govern every word
Rem below — but a machine whose whole design is that there is no seed to
Rem create is the wrong place to document the word that creates one. It
Rem lives in math.shoddy, among the other arithmetic primitives, and
Rem calling it there makes Random, RandomRange, RandomInt, Shuffle and
Rem Sample reproducible from that point on.

Rem ---- this machine's own words --------------------------------------

Def Random() As Number
    Rnd()

Def RandomRange(lo As Number, hi As Number) As Number
    If hi < lo Then
        Error("RANDOMRANGE: HI < LO")
    Else
        lo + Random() * (hi - lo)

Def RandomInt(lo As Number, hi As Number) As Number
    If hi < lo Then
        Error("RANDOMINT: HI < LO")
    Else
        lo + Floor(Random() * (hi - lo + 1))

Rem ---- shuffling and sampling ---------------------------------------
Rem Impure like everything above — each call is a fresh draw. These
Rem live here rather than in stats.shoddy because stats is pure and
Rem random.shoddy owns the Rnd edge.

Rem The list without its k-th element (local helper; no includes here).
Def DropAt(xs As List Of t, k As Number) As List Of t
    If k = 1 Then
        Rest(xs)
    Else
        Prepend(First(xs), DropAt(Rest(xs), k - 1))

Rem A uniformly random permutation: pick an element, shuffle the rest.
Def Shuffle(xs As List Of t) As List Of t
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        { }
    Else
        Let k = RandomInt(1, Length(xs))
        Prepend(Nth(xs, k), Shuffle(DropAt(xs, k)))

Rem n distinct draws without replacement (all of xs, shuffled, if n
Rem meets or exceeds the length).
Def Sample(xs As List Of t, n As Number) As List Of t
    If n <= 0 Or IsEmpty(xs) Then
        { }
    Else
        Let k = RandomInt(1, Length(xs))
        Prepend(Nth(xs, k), Sample(DropAt(xs, k), n - 1))
